# Stripe Connect readiness — one shared check

## Keep payment flows separate

| Flow | Money path | Checkout |
|---|---|---|
| Rent | Tenant → Landlord | `rent-payment-checkout` / `rentStripeCheckout.ts` |
| Invoice | Landlord/Admin → Vendor | `invoice-payment-checkout` |

Do **not** merge these into one checkout. Destinations, payers, and ledgers differ.

## Share readiness (and destination loading)

Everyone asks “is this Stripe Connect account ready?” through one rule:

**Ready = valid `acct_…` id AND `chargesEnabled === true`**

| Runtime | API |
|---|---|
| Edge | `isStripeConnectReady` / `loadLandlordStripeDestination` / `loadVendorStripeDestination` in `_shared/stripeConnect.ts` |
| Client | same names in `src/lib/stripeConnectReady.ts` |

## Do not

- Inline `acct_` + `charges_enabled` checks in new checkout or onboarding code
- Duplicate landlord vs vendor readiness predicates with different rules
- Use landlord Connect for vendor invoice payouts (or vice versa)
